snapshot-boot (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=low

  * Plymouth theme: the LUKS passphrase prompt and its bullets are visible.
    The callbacks stored their sprites in prompt, bullets and message, names
    that existed nowhere at the top level of the script, so each call made
    them local and the sprites were freed, and taken off the screen, as the
    call returned. An encrypted install showed only the lockup and the rule
    while the initramfs waited for a passphrase. The hashes are now created
    at the top level; boot messages and questions had the same fault.
  * Bullets are small signal-red squares cut from rule.png instead of text,
    capped at 60% of the screen width, so keystrokes show even when no font
    renders. Text that renders empty is not drawn, and the line height falls
    back to a size taken from the screen.

 -- "Blackbird Cyber, LLC" <293711495+matthew-blackbird-cyber@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:14:42 -0400

